When to call `refine.run()`: after a repeated failure, a reusable tactic emerges, a repeated delegation role should become a subagent spec, a repeated procedure should become a skill, a durable fact/preference should become a memory, a narrow behavioral policy should become a prompt addendum, a user corrects behavior that should persist locally or globally, validation shows a continual harness entry is wrong, or a skill/subagent/memory/prompt note should be created, updated, deleted, or rolled back. Keep `refine.run()` continual harness edits small and evidence-backed.
